From: DaffyDabz <daffydabz@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 13:03:36 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 007/371] pirates: world - spawn points, doors, tunnels, lights
 (Sept 2026 family-server fixes)

- DistributedInstanceBaseAI: Port Royal spawn nodes all carry Index -1, so
  every pirate spawned on one point; a missing or negative index now takes
  the next free slot.
- DistributedDoorBase: stop the enter/exit fade tracks when a door leaves
  interest mid-fade and give control back to the pirate.
- DistributedGATunnel: ignore a floor event when the entry locator is missing.
- WorldCreator: dynamic lights are not treated as static geometry.
- port_royal_area_jungle_b_1: use the 'sit' anim set on the seated NPC.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 pirates/instance/DistributedInstanceBaseAI.py        |  8 +++++++-
 .../worldData/port_royal_area_jungle_b_1.py          |  2 +-
 pirates/world/DistributedDoorBase.py                 | 12 ++++++++++++
 pirates/world/DistributedGATunnel.py                 |  3 +++
 pirates/world/WorldCreator.py                        |  2 +-
 5 files changed, 24 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/pirates/instance/DistributedInstanceBaseAI.py b/pirates/instance/DistributedInstanceBaseAI.py
index 136bb5a..6dec69e 100644
--- a/pirates/instance/DistributedInstanceBaseAI.py
+++ b/pirates/instance/DistributedInstanceBaseAI.py
@@ -74,7 +74,13 @@ class DistributedInstanceBaseAI(DistributedObjectAI, WorldNodeAI):
 
     def addSpawnPt(self, area, spawnPt, index=None):
         self.spawnPts[area] = self.spawnPts.setdefault(area, {})
-        self.spawnPts[area][index or len(self.spawnPts[area])] = spawnPt
+        # Family patch: Port Royal spawn nodes all carry Index -1, so keying on the index put every
+        # spawn on one point. A missing or negative index takes the next free slot instead.
+        if index is None or index < 0:
+            index = len(self.spawnPts[area])
+            while index in self.spawnPts[area]:
+                index += 1
+        self.spawnPts[area][index] = spawnPt
 
     def removeSpawnPt(self, area, index):
         if area not in self.spawnPts:
